# CODEOWNERS
#
# The enrichment workflow reads this file to name the team that owns the code an
# issue concerns, and says so in its routing comment. Every rule below is
# commented out, so until you add your own, routing comments say that no owning
# team is configured.
#
# Point rules at teams or users that exist in your organization. GitHub silently
# ignores owners it cannot resolve, so run the "Factory doctor" workflow after
# editing: it reports syntax errors and unknown owners.
#
# Syntax: https://docs.github.com/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# Examples (replace with your own paths and teams):
#
# *                     @your-org/platform-team
# /src/payments/        @your-org/payments-team
# /docs/                @your-org/docs-team
# /.github/             @your-org/platform-team
